<title>BELGIUM: Belgium reforms securities clearing system.</title>
<headline>Belgium reforms securities clearing system.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Belgian government said in a statement on Friday it had approved a draft law for the reform of the country's securities clearing system.</p>
<p>Under the new system, the Interprofessional Securities Clearing and Deposit Fund (CIK) will manage clearing of stock and debt issues by the private sector, while the Belgian central bank will do the same job for all public sector securities.</p>
<p>The draft law is based on an agreement between the central bank, the CIK and the Belgian Banking Association.</p>
